#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128880 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c28b8ae-71ef-5d26-895a-5d949fc5b164" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "6bba4758-678a-5bf6-b9df-cdc2662ab306" :question/math-academy-id "e-5525" :question/problem "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/3e677aa7f2db1cc637e0566a60813ebae1e2bccf80325106317c1d2b7717c2a5.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/67a421166c674275ae14da43962c8e5c8ea37b6a9c8a0548d5b09428b703d831.png) are the real and imaginary parts of the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/fde83769f627e95f5dfe3285bf275ebfe1678710a36c264b6662248063470bb0.png) then what is the value of $ad+eh?$" :question/worked-solution "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2-3\\text{i} & -5-7\\text{i} \\\\ 1-6\\text{i} & 5-9\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -7 \\\\ -6 & -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $a=2,d=5,e=-3$ and $h=-9.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nad+eh=2 \\cdot 5 + (-3) \\cdot (-9) = 37.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128881 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2e7753-83f4-5826-a04f-89616d34c578" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations to a Complex Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "0f32e78f-a13d-5e81-ba64-bff28a61aacf" :question/math-academy-id "e-5526" :question/problem "Given the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/766ddf98a05c69ef0791858a7f32457425cf1a9650d2205227ffc7d9d173d2e7.png) find the result of applying to $A$ the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\nR_1 := \\dfrac{1}{\\textrm{i}}R_1, \\qquad R_2 := R_2 - 2\\textrm{i}R_1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the row operations to $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} & -\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\, &  & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{\\text{i}}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\, &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2\\text{i}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/9fef320d53c15c2820719bb1d0dfabb00afa6200b43279e3137fbb25c4e67e2d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128909 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83fad21d-6b36-5198-a13f-362d34342475" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Complex Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "27f2c303-b9a9-5337-bcea-865a9273b35b" :question/math-academy-id "e-5902" :question/problem "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/b696bb055794a4ff94c86abc39ef3929113f82683b548a933fc1103245eff3fc.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/e6a5f5644ae4bcdfca4ca26bb258f33378381737ee036142c1e1c24f568ad2ed.png), then what is $AB?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the matrices using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} & \\text{i} \\\\ 1 & 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-\\text{i})\\cdot (1+2\\text{i})+\\text{i}\\cdot \\text{i} & (-\\text{i})\\cdot (1-\\text{i})+\\text{i}\\cdot 2 \\\\ 1\\cdot (1+2\\text{i})+2\\text{i}\\cdot \\text{i} & 1\\cdot (1-\\text{i})+2\\text{i}\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(2-\\text{i})+(-1) & (-1-\\text{i})+2\\text{i} \\\\ (1+2\\text{i})+(-2) & (1-\\text{i})+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -1+\\text{i} \\\\ -1+2\\text{i} & 1+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128910 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7c1b7ad-e4bf-55b2-8665-2cf35e402946" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "e8bc731b-bb0b-5a07-89d9-6acc9beebc82" :question/math-academy-id "e-5903" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overline{A},$ where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/25ce0cd375da320d1615cf49f659ec33e4646cf6bc66455198bec5fd591b3dd3.png) What is the value of $b_{11} + b_{23}?$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}4\\text{i} & 3-\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2-2\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & 1+2\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & 3\\text{i} & 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{4\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{3-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{1+\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{2-2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{1+2\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{3\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4\\text{i} & 3+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 2+\\text{i} & 1-2\\text{i} \\\\ -\\text{i} & -3\\text{i} & -2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b_{11} + b_{23} = (-4\\textrm{i}) + (1-2\\textrm{i}) = 1-6\\textrm{i}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7c1b7ad-e4bf-55b2-8665-2cf35e402946" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b607204-3b71-53ac-939b-97916fddbcb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+2\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324358} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f1db1c-1408-5c95-8af2-114a0e588129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4-\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324359} {:answer/id #uuid "5c5f8f60-af7f-5233-8fb3-cd5238d02238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4-3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324360} {:answer/id #uuid "d1cf9233-3c2b-5766-b25a-91bf96a281ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324361} {:answer/id #uuid "a2756e6f-1152-56bb-8f00-db1640ed931f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2756e6f-1152-56bb-8f00-db1640ed931f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324362} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa9f7864-75ef-56d9-8527-590262e0dd29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f578d3d-41e3-55d4-9830-a0a290e876eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-131184" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-4-2\\text{i} & 7+5\\text{i} & 6+6\\text{i} \\\\ -4+5\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & 3 \\\\ -2-\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & -3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].$\nWhat is the value of ${b}_{23}+{b}_{33}?$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-4-2\\text{i} & 7+5\\text{i} & 6+6\\text{i} \\\\ -4+5\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & 3 \\\\ -2-\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & -3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-4-2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{7+5\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{6+6\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-4+5\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{3} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-2-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-3\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4+2\\text{i} & 7-5\\text{i} & 6-6\\text{i} \\\\ -4-5\\text{i} & 2+\\text{i} & 3 \\\\ -2+\\text{i} & 2+\\text{i} & 3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{23}+{b}_{33}=3+3\\text{i}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324363 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7c1b7ad-e4bf-55b2-8665-2cf35e402946" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce4911be-3be0-53d9-b195-c5cab31cc7f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324365} {:answer/id #uuid "4cbb250e-ac90-58c9-86d6-4ef764cd58c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5-6\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324366} {:answer/id #uuid "f65c5501-d313-53d0-99fa-4b8b62b1daf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4-9\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324367} {:answer/id #uuid "da8522a5-5248-5840-9a65-6d42976c4163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8-\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324368} {:answer/id #uuid "5909fa94-4cc6-5ea7-8f1d-f3b5f1eccf12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cbb250e-ac90-58c9-86d6-4ef764cd58c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5-6\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324366} :answer-field/id #uuid "029e450b-e607-5aad-807f-cbafb42180c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84a32f02-afe1-5d8c-b768-3d299040cd8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-132715" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3\\text{i} & -2+2\\text{i} & 5-5\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & -1+5\\text{i} & -3+4\\text{i} \\\\ -5-3\\text{i} & 4-4\\text{i} & 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].$ What is the value of ${b}_{12}+{b}_{23}?$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}3\\text{i} & -2+2\\text{i} & 5-5\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & -1+5\\text{i} & -3+4\\text{i} \\\\ -5-3\\text{i} & 4-4\\text{i} & 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{3\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-2+2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{5-5\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-1+5\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-3+4\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-5-3\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{4-4\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{4\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} & -2-2\\text{i} & 5+5\\text{i} \\\\ -\\text{i} & -1-5\\text{i} & -3-4\\text{i} \\\\ -5+3\\text{i} & 4+4\\text{i} & -4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{12}+{b}_{23}=(-2-2\\text{i})+(-3-4\\text{i})=-5-6\\text{i}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c28b8ae-71ef-5d26-895a-5d949fc5b164" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "673b6dfb-5083-5a4f-89ea-12b63fa859e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324372} {:answer/id #uuid "60fed398-d7bf-519c-b3e7-8fda40137e90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324373} {:answer/id #uuid "a39d5286-93e3-5b05-8c15-15960aadda48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324374} {:answer/id #uuid "da2a18c1-0bc7-5c9c-b1cd-5e6a25374f60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324375} {:answer/id #uuid "a5d04671-591b-5177-8af9-cea1325f77f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da2a18c1-0bc7-5c9c-b1cd-5e6a25374f60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324375} :answer-field/id #uuid "12b9602e-bc40-5da4-9be1-5e4fdf17ca2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca327574-43bc-569c-875e-521409f74d08" :question/math-academy-id "q-140325" :question/problem "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}e & f \\\\ g & h\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3-9\\text{i} & -7+\\text{i} \\\\ -5-2\\text{i} & -4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ then what is the value of $bc-ef?$" :question/worked-solution "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-3-9\\text{i} & -7+\\text{i} \\\\ -5-2\\text{i} & -4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ A & =[\\begin{aligned}-3-9\\text{i} & -7+\\text{i} \\\\ -5-2\\text{i} & 0-4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -7 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $b=-7,c=-5,e=-9$ and $f=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nbc-ef=(-7)\\cdot (-5)-(-9)\\cdot 1=44.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83fad21d-6b36-5198-a13f-362d34342475" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Complex Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66657ccc-05cb-5c0b-b007-1daf83a962dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1+4\\text{i} \\\\ 4+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324379} {:answer/id #uuid "df751b5b-1409-5397-8049-9e4f2958f6c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+4\\text{i} \\\\ 4-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324380} {:answer/id #uuid "3a6d7ffa-507f-5ab0-b467-7e3c651276df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1-4\\text{i} \\\\ 4+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324381} {:answer/id #uuid "b1bcc2ec-3f0a-543a-aae2-e70fba163efe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+4\\text{i} \\\\ -1+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324382} {:answer/id #uuid "515320af-da9e-5c86-9c3e-b1a76f31af2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4+\\text{i} \\\\ -1+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "515320af-da9e-5c86-9c3e-b1a76f31af2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4+\\text{i} \\\\ -1+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324383} :answer-field/id #uuid "f590a31e-f5c5-5f40-b354-7534b9143fa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "163c6193-9af2-56e7-a390-ebdee1bcfd43" :question/math-academy-id "q-140328" :question/problem "If $\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & 3-\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i} & 1+2\\text{i} & 1+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ -\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$, then $\\,Ax=$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the matrix by the vector using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & 3-\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i} & 1+2\\text{i} & 1+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} \\\\ -\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(1-\\text{i})(\\text{i})+(2-\\text{i})(-\\text{i})+(3-\\text{i})(1+\\text{i}) \\\\ (1+\\text{i})(\\text{i})+(1+2\\text{i})(-\\text{i})+(1+3\\text{i})(1+\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(1+\\text{i})+(-1-2\\text{i})+(4+2\\text{i}) \\\\ (-1+\\text{i})+(2-\\text{i})+(-2+4\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4+\\text{i} \\\\ -1+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129584 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83fad21d-6b36-5198-a13f-362d34342475" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Complex Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c5d8ed4-6f75-5082-b7b7-e39a54276598" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}39 - 9\\textrm{i} \\\\ 12 - 9\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127299} {:answer/id #uuid "16f557a6-39d9-5b39-a9aa-ab154dca7263" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 - 9\\textrm{i} \\\\ 12 - 39\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127300} {:answer/id #uuid "578b04be-f905-5c8b-8f9f-283e54851964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 - 9\\textrm{i} \\\\ 9 - 39\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127301} {:answer/id #uuid "5b983f8a-6bbe-5556-ae72-b38aaaa023bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 - 39\\textrm{i} \\\\ 12 - 9\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127302} {:answer/id #uuid "6c435021-c56e-50de-9ee9-20fd7f0d3480" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 - 12\\textrm{i} \\\\ 9 - 39\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16f557a6-39d9-5b39-a9aa-ab154dca7263" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 - 9\\textrm{i} \\\\ 12 - 39\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127300} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a714f41-0298-507c-8466-ccc6890e1e14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127298}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2ea38d57-a4a8-5d67-9d86-a30132652825" :question/math-academy-id "q-38391" :question/problem "If $\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & 2-2\\text{i} \\\\ 3-6\\text{i} & 3-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5-2\\text{i} \\\\ 2+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$, then $\\,Ax=$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the matrix by the vector using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & 2-2\\text{i} \\\\ 3-6\\text{i} & 3-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5-2\\text{i} \\\\ 2+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(1-\\text{i})(5-2\\text{i})+(2-2\\text{i})(2+\\text{i}) \\\\ (3-6\\text{i})(5-2\\text{i})+(3-3\\text{i})(2+\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(3-7\\text{i})+(6-2\\text{i}) \\\\ (3-36\\text{i})+(9-3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9-9\\text{i} \\\\ 12-39\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129585 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83fad21d-6b36-5198-a13f-362d34342475" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Complex Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89eb823d-db43-584e-899b-b026793b36f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}17\\textrm{i} & -1 \\\\ 19\\textrm{i} & 3 + 20\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127305} {:answer/id #uuid "90b308ae-b2dd-558f-99d5-3abf5d9bac0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 + 13\\textrm{i} & -14 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ 9\\textrm{i} & 20 + 3\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127306} {:answer/id #uuid "bfe75f2f-4b31-55b4-92f7-4d6f358a3f21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 + 17\\textrm{i} & -1 + 14\\textrm{i} \\\\ 19\\textrm{i} & 3 + 20\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127307} {:answer/id #uuid "ff76c128-4299-5e0b-a95c-7c3d76e3f052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 + 17\\textrm{i} & -1 + 14\\textrm{i} \\\\ -2 + 19\\textrm{i} & 20\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127308} {:answer/id #uuid "282925cc-5df7-5cfd-bd40-6ffff3b6147d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 + 7\\textrm{i} & -1 + 4\\textrm{i} \\\\ 19\\textrm{i} & 3 - 12\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfe75f2f-4b31-55b4-92f7-4d6f358a3f21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 + 17\\textrm{i} & -1 + 14\\textrm{i} \\\\ 19\\textrm{i} & 3 + 20\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127307} :answer-field/id #uuid "9166f064-77a9-5205-ae9d-158d1aeae952" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c632a1a7-d3f4-5920-9d3f-59ab7769775e" :question/math-academy-id "q-38392" :question/problem "If $\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}2+3\\text{i} & 1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 2+\\text{i} & 4+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3+2\\text{i} & 2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1+2\\text{i} & 2+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$, then $AB=$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the matrices using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}2+3\\text{i} & 1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 2+\\text{i} & 4+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3+2\\text{i} & 2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1+2\\text{i} & 2+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(2+3\\text{i})(3+2\\text{i})+(1+2\\text{i})(1+2\\text{i}) & (2+3\\text{i})(2+\\text{i})+(1+2\\text{i})(2+2\\text{i}) \\\\ (2+\\text{i})(3+2\\text{i})+(4+4\\text{i})(1+2\\text{i}) & (2+\\text{i})(2+\\text{i})+(4+4\\text{i})(2+2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}13\\text{i}+(-3+4\\text{i}) & (1+8\\text{i})+(-2+6\\text{i}) \\\\ (4+7\\text{i})+(-4+12\\text{i}) & (3+4\\text{i})+16\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+17\\text{i} & -1+14\\text{i} \\\\ 19\\text{i} & 3+20\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c28b8ae-71ef-5d26-895a-5d949fc5b164" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b79f7c-7410-5306-80d8-c6112085a466" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -7 \\\\ 4 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127317} {:answer/id #uuid "1a022ea5-a4a2-5c15-b2a5-c21bb97ab959" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127318} {:answer/id #uuid "51ca3a46-7338-5a8a-a5e2-bd8c158424be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127319} {:answer/id #uuid "5a535877-3598-581c-8c5e-d701455ba892" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127320} {:answer/id #uuid "7c9e6b6b-adfe-5204-8580-54abd9d22f09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -7 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a535877-3598-581c-8c5e-d701455ba892" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127320} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb553eb4-b19a-577e-a7e3-36d38b0f5451" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bd10f116-420a-5abf-b912-c6a791dc88fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-38397" :question/problem "Find the real part of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2+3\\text{i} & -5+2\\text{i} \\\\ 6-7\\text{i} & 4-9\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-2+3\\text{i} & -5+2\\text{i} \\\\ 6-7\\text{i} & 4-9\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -5 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -7 & -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{Re}(A)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -5 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324384 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2e7753-83f4-5826-a04f-89616d34c578" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations to a Complex Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc69e95c-9ffc-5136-979b-a6e501c03190" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324386} {:answer/id #uuid "85136190-d522-5bdc-966e-a69dc00cd155" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\text{i}+2 \\\\ -2\\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324387} {:answer/id #uuid "b76e69c9-5dff-5606-b38f-3366e3d2908b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\text{i} & \\text{i}-2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324388} {:answer/id #uuid "02a4ee48-dfef-5e10-9b2e-90ef939d5746" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 4\\text{i} & \\text{i}+2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324389} {:answer/id #uuid "ffa86dfc-0076-595a-8b2e-71754ba0e58c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & \\text{i}+2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffa86dfc-0076-595a-8b2e-71754ba0e58c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & \\text{i}+2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324390} :answer-field/id #uuid "578a8f31-ff42-55ab-a6c7-f1067b860d74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ea3a8a38-8a00-5f57-b578-5a4b0637d9c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-39005" :question/problem "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ -2\\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$, find the result of applying to $A$ the following elementary row operation:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{2\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}}{R}_{1}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the row operations to $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ -2\\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{2\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ -2\\text{i}+\\frac{2\\text{i}(1+\\text{i})}{1+\\text{i}} & \\text{i}+\\frac{2\\text{i}(1-\\text{i})}{1+\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ -2\\text{i}+2\\text{i} & \\text{i}+\\frac{2(\\text{i}+1)}{1+\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & \\text{i}+2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result  is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & \\text{i}+2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129647 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2e7753-83f4-5826-a04f-89616d34c578" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations to a Complex Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "937e7ecb-5d77-505e-a76c-46c702d21a7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127677} {:answer/id #uuid "93edd233-da7b-598a-94e0-4bdecd43e6e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\textrm{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127678} {:answer/id #uuid "ad2c84f0-ea43-59b5-9f39-f9b287c237b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127679} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc717fd-8668-5fac-880a-295a4ac24690" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ 2\\textrm{i} & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127680} {:answer/id #uuid "2e725b4a-9a4d-5c6d-af11-5472379222ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad2c84f0-ea43-59b5-9f39-f9b287c237b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127679} :answer-field/id #uuid "04cbad56-afe9-56dd-b327-d0b3664c9323" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "82b32e6d-28e5-58d1-919e-cc85298dd3c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-39014" :question/problem "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2\\text{i} & 1\\end{aligned}]$, find the result of applying to $A$ the following  elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}-1}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}={R}_{2}-2\\text{i}{R}_{1}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the row operations to $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2\\text{i} & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}-1}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2\\text{i} & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2\\text{i}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7c1b7ad-e4bf-55b2-8665-2cf35e402946" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d09af70f-46d6-5ee3-82b7-f25cb59f8d1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3-3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324393} {:answer/id #uuid "d42d0f90-35a2-5ab3-acb8-ebc49c6cc72f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324394} {:answer/id #uuid "d2dbe44b-248f-5bde-91c6-3ff9244cb56b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3+3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324395} {:answer/id #uuid "24783072-6c28-578a-8d50-e157bf0ac679" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324396} {:answer/id #uuid "a65bd6d9-764a-53cd-8f73-ec82f69e173a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a65bd6d9-764a-53cd-8f73-ec82f69e173a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324397} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca5d2b99-306b-54d5-8ccf-e10cbd555876" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b17ecbd-7ab3-5359-82f8-fd86385499df" :question/math-academy-id "q-76055" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2+\\text{i} & 4 & -\\text{i} \\\\ -5\\text{i} & 7-5\\text{i} & 1 \\\\ 3-2\\text{i} & \\text{i} & 0\\end{aligned}].$ What is the value of ${b}_{13}+{b}_{31}?$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-2+\\text{i} & 4 & -\\text{i} \\\\ -5\\text{i} & 7-5\\text{i} & 1 \\\\ 3-2\\text{i} & \\text{i} & 0\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-2+\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{4} & \\overset{―}{-\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-5\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{7-5\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{1} \\\\ \\overset{―}{3-2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{0}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2-\\text{i} & 4 & \\text{i} \\\\ 5\\text{i} & 7+5\\text{i} & 1 \\\\ 3+2\\text{i} & -\\text{i} & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{13}+{b}_{31}=\\text{i}+(3+2\\text{i})=3+3\\text{i}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324398 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7c1b7ad-e4bf-55b2-8665-2cf35e402946" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5ab1397-1508-5917-9175-f478087ddc1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324400} {:answer/id #uuid "f5633dd5-5eea-5a0a-8958-75fb99f9eb48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218632440